Distance from major town: Approximately half an hour north of Launceston.
Social Media: Mentions of Facebook and Instagram are made by Visit Northern Tasmania.

## Notable / Distinctive
Brook Eden Vineyard is a small, family-owned, and hand-tended vineyard. Its location at 41º South, within the Pipers River region, positions it as a "viticulture on-the-edge" site, contributing to one of Australia's longest ripening seasons. This extended ripening period is credited with producing fruit of exceptional flavor and aroma. The vineyard's commitment to sustainable practices includes maintaining unirrigated vines and fostering a natural wetland habitat where platypus can be observed. Brook Eden is also notable for being a founding member of the Tamar Wine Tourism Route and for its philosophy of holding an impressive inventory of vintages to offer matured wines to patrons. The planting of Lagrein is a relatively new and potentially distinctive addition to Tasmanian viticulture.

